# GitHub's Linguist (the language-stats bar on the repo page) guesses a .h
# file's language from its content, since the extension alone is ambiguous
# between C, C++ and Objective-C. A header with few C++-only tokens (no
# class/namespace/template/::) can get misclassified as plain C — this
# project's headers are all C++, so tell Linguist that outright rather than
# leaving it to guess per file.
*.h linguist-language=C++
